WEBVTT

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.090
Wait!

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.930
Thief!

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.020
Someone help...

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:47.800
Hey!

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.920
You like running?

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:53.980
Huh?

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.700
Do you like running?

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:57.990
What?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.000
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.420
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.420
This is Nira the dog.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.640
<b>201</b>

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.640
Let me introduce you.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.280
These are the Jo brothers from room 201.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.000
The older brother's Jotaro.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.250
Call me Jota.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.380
The younger brother's Jojiro.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.440
I'm Joji.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.730
Nice to meet you.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.030
205

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.450
The Karakara-tei public baths!

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.090
Sugiyama Takashi from room 205.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.510
He's a third-year business school student.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.160
His nickname is Shindo.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.880
Shindo's written with the
characters for "god" and "child."

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.410
Nice to meet you.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:13.870
Back there is Sakaguchi Yohei of room 205.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.360
He's a sociology student.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.230
Like me, he's a fourth-year.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.810
Call him "King."

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.600
1938!

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.840
He's the king of trivia.
 Self-proclaimed, that is.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.350
<b>204
 Do Not Enter</b>

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.190
Don't touch that!

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.580
It's all exquisitely balanced.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.990
I can't be held responsible
for anything that happens.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.240
You heard him.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.430
That's Kashiwazaki Akane of room 204.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.010
He's a second-year literature student.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.200
His nickname is "Prince."

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.710
<b>104</b>

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.510
That's Hirata Akihiro from room 104.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.710
We call him Nico-chan Senpai.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.370
He's a nicotine addict!

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.670
He's a third-year science
and engineering student.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.640
How many times do I have to say it?

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.780
He was a year above me when I first met him,

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.780
but now he's a year behind me.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.760
It stinks! It really, really stinks!

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.080
Shut up. You're just too high-strung.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.230
<b>102</b>

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.000
If I sue, there's a 
100 percent chance I'll win.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.280
This is Iwakura Yukihiko from room 102.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.320
We call him Yuki.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.570
Are you listening, Nico-chan Senpai?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.110
He's a fourth-year law student
who passed the bar on his first try.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.360
You're smoking another?

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.370
This is the landlord, Mr. Tazaki.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.330
This is Musa Kamara, a foreign student.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.590
He's in room 203.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.970
He's a second-year science
and engineering student.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:44.980
Nice to meet you.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.340
Let me know when you're out of the bath.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:58.060
I'm in room 101.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.620
He—

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.980
Take your time.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.140
What am I doing?

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.680
<b><i>The 10th Man</i></b>

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.680
Where did you find him?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.260
Kurahara Kakeru.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.430
He's a first-year.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.080
Kurahara?

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.390
I've heard that name before.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:40.820
Coach...

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.660
Huh?

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:44.400
That's ten.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.660
You win.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.520
Fine, then. Do what you want.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:03.040
Come on! You should listen
to your department's seniors!

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.880
Well? Huh?

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.770
Keep it down. This place is tiny.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:11.910
Quit whining. You guys have the biggest room.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:12.780
What?

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.800
There's two of us in one room.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.760
I can't hear you. What was that?

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.700
But I was about to finish.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.330
Newbie, eat something.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.900
This is your welcoming party.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:29.050
Since Haiji made it, it's all country cooking.

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:32.630
Where are you from?

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.380
I'm from Yamagata.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.980
Uh...

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.080
Oh, you don't have to tell us.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.410
I'm from Tanzania.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.330
Have you heard of Tanzania?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:44.900
Africa?

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.220
Yeah. Ever been there?

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:48.810
No.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:50.260
Most people haven't.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.400
Musa's a government-sponsored
 exchange student.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.580
He's smart.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.860
Isn't his Japanese incredible?

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.340
It's not that good...

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.150
Don't, guys!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.440
You're too close!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.030
To being fully occupied!

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:15.060
A toast to our tenth resident!

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.950
Cheers!

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.720
That's good! It stings!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.080
You should definitely read it.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:29.690
It's no exaggeration to say it'll
completely change your college life.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:30.700
Really?

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.690
Let us borrow that comic, then.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.460
Buy it yourself.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.410
Why can't I wear my jacket?

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.280
You'd stand out as the only one.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.570
Do I really need a suit?

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:44.600
No one wears jeans when
 they're looking for a job.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.650
King, what did you do for your
coming-of-age ceremony?

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.790
Huh? I didn't attend.

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:52.510
Did your high school uniform include a blazer?

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.620
You're not telling me to wear that, are you?

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.110
Here.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.850
How'd you guys meet?

00:07:58.850 --> 00:07:59.660
Huh?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.080
You and Haiji.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.740
You spilled on yourself, Jota.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.090
Hold still.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:08.560
Stop laughing.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:10.420
We ran into each other on the street.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.130
Really?

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:16.300
You're Haiji's long-awaited tenth man.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.540
We were worried about who'd show up.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.100
We figured he'd bring someone ridiculous.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.500
I'm glad you seem decent.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.020
What are you discussing with the newbie?

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:32.950
Let us join in.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:33.960
What?

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.570
We're discussing how to tell you two apart.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.370
What?

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:39.320
Which one am I?

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.080
Who am I, newbie?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.010
What?

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:46.360
Get this question right,
and you'll win a can of beer.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.000
But I'm underage.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.960
I know! Jota!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.760
Why'd <i>you</i> answer the question?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.290
You think I wouldn't answer a quiz question?

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.890
What's this?

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.230
Why'd you have to find that, Shindo?

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:05.270
I knew I felt a breeze.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.280
Haiji, they made a hole in the floor.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.330
Hush! It's a secret!

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.700
It's only been ten days since they moved in.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:16.000
It's fine. Just cover it up with a magazine.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.070
Don't let the landlord find out.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.510
All right!

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.700
Hey, wait! You can't use that issue!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.330
I'm saving it forever!

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.650
You scared me.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.270
What was that for?

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.150
I know the party's in full swing,
but lend me your ears.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:56.470
It's important.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.540
Is it a girl?

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.450
You finally got a girlfriend?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.600
We're all ears, Haiji.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:03.570
It's not that.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.680
Since Kurahara moved in,
there are finally ten of us.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.860
What? I haven't decided to move in yet.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:15.990
What?

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.730
There are exactly ten of us.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.800
You've been saying that ever
since the twins moved in.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.720
"Just one more, just one more..."

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.240
Those cursed words.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:28.360
You must be glad we filled
the last room surprisingly quickly.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.610
Yeah. It's not enough to just think about it.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.600
You should always state your wishes out loud.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:37.310
You've got to seize your own destiny.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:39.740
I don't know what you're talking about,

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:43.940
but why don't we take a trip somewhere
to celebrate reaching ten?

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:45.210
Good idea.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.370
We can stay at an inn and drink sake.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.330
That's not any different from right now.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.130
Take a trip together... Sounds nice.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.900
Right? Where should we go?

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:00.350
I know the perfect place.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.890
Where?

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:03.630
Hakone.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.570
Well, yeah, I guess.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:11.730
They've got hot springs,
and it's easy to get there.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.570
Nice idea, Haiji.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.800
Should we take the train or rent a car?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.190
We won't take a vehicle.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.150
We'll use our legs to get around.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.150
Huh? What?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.910
Let's aim for the top together.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:30.300
Everyone's seen it at least once on
New Year's while eating rice-cake soup.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.820
Let's run it together.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.920
The Hakone Ekiden.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.940
You still only get in for a second, Haiji.

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:59.050
It's been three years,
but I still can't get used to the heat.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:03.150
So you're a fourth-year now, huh?

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:04.910
Time flies.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:07.870
How's the Chikusei-so?

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:09.420
What do you mean?

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.080
Isn't it obvious?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.160
"Just one more."

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.930
Your first and final chance
must've arrived, right?

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:17.360
Not yet.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.420
Well, the new students will be coming soon.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:25.150
I'm sure you'll find someone.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.130
<b>Public Bath</b>

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:41.990
Your first and final chance must've arrived, right?

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.520
Just one more.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:52.750
Hey, wait!

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:04.900
Wait!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:12.930
Wait!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.070
Thief!

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:17.900
Someone help...

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:38.410
Hey!

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:40.750
You like running?

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:42.930
Huh?

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.380
Do you like running?

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.080
What?

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:58.550
Don't suddenly stop like that.

00:13:58.550 --> 00:13:59.690
Let's have a chat.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.120
What?

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.110
Why did you shoplift?

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.030
<b>Tea</b>

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:20.200
I won't call the cops. I promise.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.240
I just want to know who you are.

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:27.820
I'm Kiyose Haiji, a fourth-year
 literature student at Kansei University.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.120
Who are you?

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:33.970
Kurahara Kakeru.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:35.750
Kurahara...

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:39.320
Where's your home? Do you live around here?

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.810
No, uh... I'm at Kansei University.

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:45.380
You're a Kansei University student?

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.180
Which department?

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:47.700
Seriously, I—

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.740
I definitely can't ignore you
if you're an underclassman!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.240
Which department are you in?

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.990
Sociology.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.950
Can I go now?

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.780
Wait.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.290
What?

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.850
Are you broke? What about your allowance?

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:05.820
I lost my entire apartment
deposit at a mah-jong parlor.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:06.630
Come to my place.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.110
What?

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:10.440
I'll show you the apartment where I live.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:12.300
There's an empty room.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.180
But I don't have any money.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.600
You can pay when you can.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:19.170
Trust me. I'll make it work.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.800
We'll start with the convenience store.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.360
Let's go apologize.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.320
This is it.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:35.990
The Chikusei-so. We call it Aotake.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:40.080
That's the landlord's house.
We'll go see him later.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.090
<b>103</b>

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.760
Room 103. This is your room.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.190
There's no curfew.

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:59.100
I'll get you a futon tomorrow, so you'll
have to make do with my blanket tonight.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.110
I'll introduce you to the guys.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.290
Let's run it together.

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.180
The Hakone Ekiden.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.880
But, uh... what?

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.540
What are you talking about?

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:44.020
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.100
That's the sign out front.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.940
<b>Kansei University
 Track and Field Club</b>

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.400
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:53.860
"Kansei University Track and Field Club...

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.860
<b>Track and Field Club</b>

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.820
<b>Training Camp</b>

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.820
...Training Camp?!"

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.330
What?!

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.860
When did you add that?

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:03.040
Does this degradation look recent to you?

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:06.040
It was so dirty, we couldn't read it.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.500
Hold on, Haiji.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:08.420
The Ekiden?

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.030
The marathon?

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:11.630
Isn't it a relay race?

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.160
This is the Kansei University Track
and Field Club member dorm.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:16.380
In other words,

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:21.600
you're now members of the 
Kansei University Track and Field Club.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.520
What?!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:33.490
I never signed up for that!

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.900
Moving in here signs you up for the club.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:38.270
Didn't you find it strange
that in this day and age

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:41.620
the rent's 30,000 yen, and we
 serve breakfast and dinner?

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.140
Isn't this a scam?

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.260
How did you not know about this?

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:46.960
What?

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.510
Haven't you been living here longer than Haiji?

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:53.090
But the old man never told me anything.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:59.550
I can't believe my first job after passing
the bar will be my own civil trial.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.300
Don't bother trying to sue me.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.470
Your rental application
is your club application.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:05.760
Are we registered?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.190
Are we registered with the
Inter-University Athletic Union of Kanto?

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.650
Of course we are.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.360
Who's the coach?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.320
Our landlord, Tazaki Genichiro.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.570
What?!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.280
What?

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.440
The old man?

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.680
Seriously?

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.060
But he's so decrepit.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.450
Don't be rude.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.410
The landlord was known as the treasure
of the Japan Association of Athletics.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:32.260
By the time Tsuburaya Kokichi wrote
his food-based suicide note and died,

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:37.020
the landlord was already considered
Kansei University's great coach.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.430
There's no trace of his incredible nature left.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.290
You sure know a lot about him, newbie.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:46.560
What's the Inter-University Athletic...

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:47.420
I see.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.240
He must mean the 
Kanto Gogakuren from <i>Otokojuku</i>.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.730
With over a thousand members,
they're led by Date Omito.

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:56.600
I don't think that's right.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.190
We can't.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.200
Not Hakone.

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:03.410
There's no way.

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:11.600
No one knows that for sure.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:53.960
Hey.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.040
Do you run every day?

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.890
So do I, while taking Nira for his walk.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:08.850
For your health?

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:10.400
No.

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:13.380
Before you ask, I'll tell you.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.020
I ran in high school.

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.200
I'm almost back at full speed.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.940
In six months, I'll be
 able to match your pace.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.500
What are you talking about?

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:28.820
I'm serious.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:35.120
I'm going to run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:37.930
Starting today, I'm going
to win over all the guys.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:42.290
That includes you,

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.030
Sendai Josei High School graduate

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.370
Kurahara Kakeru.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:42.830
Next time: "The Ogre's Arrival."

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>Next Time: The Ogre's Arrival</b>
